Bloom: evaluate __has_include_next in the MSVC stdatomic.h compat header only under clang.

The header chose clang-cl's own stdatomic.h with
`#if defined(__clang__) && __has_include_next(<stdatomic.h>)`. MSVC defines no
__has_include_next, and from compiler version 19.52 its preprocessor rejects the
expression even though defined(__clang__) has already made it false (error C7780,
"function-like macro '__has_include_next' is not defined", then fatal error C1017).
The test now sits in an #if nested inside `#if defined(__clang__)`, which MSVC skips
without evaluating, and sets a local macro that selects the same branch as before.
Every compiler that accepted the unmodified header takes the branch it took before.

Upstream fixed the same failure after 1.5.4 by defining a fallback __has_include_next
(VideoLAN dav1d commit a34e0685b9111b9eb1d7835ea7bea5b425dced73, released in 1.5.5).

--- a/include/compat/msvc/stdatomic.h
+++ b/include/compat/msvc/stdatomic.h
@@ -32,7 +32,15 @@
 #pragma warning(push)
 #pragma warning(disable:4067)    /* newline for __has_include_next */
 
-#if defined(__clang__) && __has_include_next(<stdatomic.h>)
+/* MSVC 19.52 rejects __has_include_next in an #if expression even when
+ * defined(__clang__) has already made it false, so only clang evaluates it. */
+#if defined(__clang__)
+#  if __has_include_next(<stdatomic.h>)
+#    define DAV1D_COMPAT_MSVC_CLANG_STDATOMIC_H 1
+#  endif
+#endif
+
+#if defined(DAV1D_COMPAT_MSVC_CLANG_STDATOMIC_H)
    /* use the clang stdatomic.h with clang-cl*/
 #  include_next <stdatomic.h>
 #else /* ! stdatomic.h */
